  "reviewReply": "I reviewed Run `0ca3abe6-40d2-4d0a-a0b8-f2486ef774ad` (status: completed, not a fixture).\n\n## What went well\n- Research actually invoked `research-topics@1` (key `habits`, 1 call, completed) and quoted the returned reference ID `TOPIC-104` exactly.\n- It delivered one practical next step as specified.\n\n## One suggested improvement (not applied)\n\n**Add a fidelity guard against out-of-scope context claims.** In the Run, Research stated: *\"This aligns with the project brief's goal of turning intentions into small, observable next actions...\"* — but Research's definition binds only `studio-research@1`; it does not hold `project-knowledge@1`, so it asserted alignment with a project brief it never actually read. That's a small hallucinated-justification risk that could mislead Quellight's relay.\n\n**Concrete suggestion:** append one line to Research's instructions, e.g.:\n\n> \"Base your answer strictly on the tool result and your research knowledge source. Do not reference, summarize, or claim alignment with project knowledge — that context belongs to the delegating agent, which handles the synthesis.\"\n\nThis keeps Research's output fully verifiable against its actual resources while leaving cross-context synthesis to Quellight.\n\nWant me to apply this edit to Research (`afb00ff0-11ae-4457-935f-fd8079319f71`)? I won't change anything until you confirm.",
